============================================================================================================
DELIVERABLE 3 -- H4: IS THE FLOOR REUSED FROM K = 8?
============================================================================================================
  BY CONSTRUCTION: `cert_rows` builds `n_inc` inside the per-pulsar loop from
  the comps IN SCOPE, and calls `recut_floor` on it in the same iteration.
  There is no floor cache and no cross-K state -- `vernier25.floor_for`'s
  _FLOOR_CACHE is for the DETECTION F-floor and is never touched here.
  Empirical confirmation: recut with a different floor RNG stream and with
  4x and 12x the nulls; a reused floor would not move, a genuine one will
  move only inside its own bootstrap error.

    n_null    f_cert   f_SCRAM  median floor  median bar  n_SCRAM
        32   0.04452   0.02359         0.431       8.565     0.75
       128   0.04452   0.01498         0.421       8.559     0.50
       384   0.05042   0.02359         0.402       8.557     0.75

  H4 VERDICT: the floor is recut every call and the leak is flat in n_null.
  H4 is DEAD -- both by construction and empirically.

