============================================================================================================
DELIVERABLE 6 -- THE REPAIR, AND THE CORRECTED K = 16 COLUMN
============================================================================================================
  The control is repaired, not the gate: the scramble must displace the comb
  OUT of the searched window and by at least a few fringes. Per pulsar the
  displacement is drawn from U(w_a, w_a + 500 pc) in magnitude with a random
  sign, where w_a = max(window half-width, 3 fringes) -- so the null tests
  'no comb in this window' for every pulsar, uniformly, instead of testing it
  only for the pulsars whose priors happen to be tighter than 500 pc.

                             variant   K    f_cert    f_true   f_SCRAM  SCRAM/sig  n_SCRAM
      banked scramble U(-500,500) pc   8   0.02101   0.02101   0.00000      0.000     0.00
    window-aware scramble (REPAIRED)   8   0.02101   0.02101   0.00862      0.410     0.25
      banked scramble U(-500,500) pc  16   0.03574   0.03318   0.01574      0.441     0.50
    window-aware scramble (REPAIRED)  16   0.03574   0.03318   0.00395      0.111     0.12

  SUB-FRINGE RULE (the brief's item 6, reported for completeness). The
  Anchor-Census convention is K <= 3 = 'anchor'. Applying it as an exclusion
  to the CERTIFICATION column at K = 16:
    pulsars at K_i <= 3 in this cell: 1; their share of the leak: 64.0 %
